Z||000005||Robert||07-09-2000||11:21 PM||||Hi jlruiz67 and all:<BR>Just got back from San Diego.  West Fest 2000 was a great success.   This was a great personal experience for me; every Fiero owner should do an event like this at least once in his or her life.  I’ve never “talked” Fiero so much in my life.<BR>It was a real eye opener for me, I thought my car looked decent, but compared to some of the cars down there, I need to do a lot of work.  I didn’t come away with a trophy, but I kept my eyes open,….. watch out for me next year.<BR>I am terrible with remembering names, so everyone please excuse me.  I remember cars better than names.  I met at least 5 people who were the original owner of their car; one had over 300,000 miles on his silver 87 GT.  I asked him how he got so many miles on his car, his reply was “ I love driving it so much, I will go 20 miles just to get some breakfast”.  <BR>I[m kinda tired right now and the computer is acting up, so I’ll just give you a hint of what went on this weekend, and get back to you later.<P>Night all<P>Robert<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheLot.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||07-09-2000||11:28 PM||||Hey Robert!! Glad you had a good time there -- I'll give you a report on Nationals in a couple of weeks. -- Nice shot of Roy!! since that is his little silver car sitting there, is that Georges next to it or, looks like the one on the other side of it is green too!! -- Would that be yours across the lot?? -- Your car looks so good (especially with the Mr. Mike's leather) I am surprised that you didn't walk away with a trophy - my guess tho is, that with the paint it threw you into the 'custom' class? That's a hard one to compete in -- that's why I am keeping mine mainly stock!! -- Anyway, glad you made it back safe and sound and you enjoyed the weekend!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
